@startuml
!theme blueprint

title LLM Challenges — Repository Overview

package "llm-challenges" {

  [README.md] as readme
  [INSTRUCTIONS.md] as instructions
  [package.json] as pkg
  [.gitignore] as gitignore

  package "Challenges" {

    [challengeNN-<slug>/\nREADME.md] as challenge_readme

    package "Challenge Types" {
      [Deep Readonly\n(types, tests, examples)] as c1
      [Solar System\n(index.html, sketch.js)] as c2
      [Repo Overview\n(overview.puml, overview.md)] as c3
    }

    challenge_readme --> c1 : "challenge01-"
    challenge_readme --> c2 : "challenge02-"
    challenge_readme --> c3 : "challenge03-"
  }

  package "LLM Solutions" {
    [harness_model_date/\nsolution files] as solutions
  }

  package "Config" {
    [node_modules/] as deps
    [package-lock.json] as lock
  }
}

' Relationships
readme ..> instructions : references
readme ..> challenge_readme : describes workflow
instructions ..> solutions : defines naming convention
pkg ..> deps : manages
lock ..> pkg : locks versions
gitignore ..> deps : excludes
challenge_readme ..> solutions : deliverables go here

note bottom of solutions
  Each LLM run creates a folder:
  [harness]_[model]_[quant]_[date]/
  containing that model's solution files.
  These are excluded from the diagram
  to keep it generic and future-proof.
end note

note right of c1
  TypeScript: DeepReadonly,
  DeepMutable, DeepPartial,
  DeepRequired, DeepPick
end note

note right of c2
  Creative coding: p5.js solar
  system with 8 planets, moons,
  zoom/pan, starfield
end note

note right of c3
  Documentation: analyse repo
  structure, produce PlantUML
  overview diagram
end note

@enduml
